{
  "baseRefOid": "a470608f91a6c1fa42a1fdde9815625715b2c1c9",
  "body": "Scoring and top-k kernels now read token IDs in their producer's integer width and layout. Repeated int64 widening and contiguous materializations are removed. Small transposed selections use a block-sized shared tile; larger selections retain the qualified native-stride program. FP32 arithmetic/order, ranks and serialized token values stay unchanged.\n\nStacked on #893. The final dispatch selects only per-case GPU programs qualified on both timing boots, with a five-standard-error upper time ratio at most 1 or verified identity with the prerequisite program. It adds no conversion buffer or GPU launch. There is no regression allowance and no unqualified-program reuse.\n\nValidation on owner-authorized idle sp8 using candidate-38 by immutable image digest:\n\n- All 120 GPU cases verified on both fresh final boots: 112 exactly match qualified v6 programs and eight exactly match the shared-stage programs qualified over 480 mirrored rounds per boot in v7. Reference code, input hashes and strides match too; every output is checked independently. No new timings are claimed for identical programs.\n- 673 correctness checks pass on each boot, including native layouts, 31/32/33 boundaries, prompt/speculative scores, wire IDs, graphs and cold startup freeze.\n- Both expanded IKET captures decode all 56 expected launches with phase ranges and warp lifetimes, explicitly exercising shared staging and aligned vector loads. Minimum sampled host memory available: 111.08 GiB, with no guard stop.\n- The full candidate-38/prerequisite/patch stack applies in a fresh tree. Composition with #885, #886 and #887 also applies cleanly (source check only). Doctor, export hashes, parsing and diff checks pass; no new lint diagnostics. Complete build inputs are not prepared locally.\n\nAll rejected sources and unfavorable observations remain in the experiment. Full-image/full-model and host enqueue performance qualification remain before promotion. Serving and promoted configuration, locks and baselines were not changed.\n\n[Experiment and complete retained evidence](https://github.com/christopherowen/spark-ds41f/tree/605828e5b83f19bdf6d71073230c68bfb4a0127e/experiments/2026-11-04-native-score-inputs).\n",
